## SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
## BusyBox's defconfig, and these lines over it (issue 1018). A line
## starting `## ` is a comment; every other line must be in the
## configuration after the merge, or the build fails.
##
## One file, with nothing to load at run time.
CONFIG_STATIC=y
## `tc` does not build against the kernel's current headers.
# CONFIG_TC is not set
## 32-bit RISC-V Linux has only the 64-bit time calls, so there is no
## settimeofday for `hwclock`, and the board has no clock for it either.
# CONFIG_HWCLOCK is not set
## The x86 SHA instructions, whose code is not guarded for other targets.
# CONFIG_SHA1_HWACCEL is not set
# CONFIG_SHA256_HWACCEL is not set
## libbb.h's BB_GLOBAL_CONST, the "const" on each applet's pointer to
## its globals, made empty: clang reads that pointer before an applet
## sets it, so awk and netstat dereferenced NULL (issue 1585). libbb.h
## names this as the switch for a toolchain that breaks the trick.
CONFIG_EXTRA_CFLAGS="-DBB_GLOBAL_CONST="
